    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-sm max-w-none text-[var(--ink-body)] leading-relaxed space-y-6">
      
      {page === 'home' && (
        <>
          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--ink-primary)] tracking-tight">
              1. What is an Online Age Calculator? (Chronological Age vs. Biological Age)
            </h3>
            <p>
              An <strong>online age calculator</strong> is a specialized digital utility designed to measure the precise duration of time elapsed between a person's <strong>date of birth</strong> and a specific reference date, such as <strong>today's date</strong> or a future examination cutoff date. Unlike informal estimates, a precision <strong>chronological age calculator</strong> factors in exact calendar math—accounting for varying month lengths (28, 30, or 31 days) and leap year intercalations.
            </p>
            <p>
              While your <strong>chronological age by date of birth free</strong> measures calendar time, other concepts like <em>biological age</em>, <em>lunar age calculator</em> values, and <em>heart age calculator</em> metrics assess health performance rather than pure calendar duration.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--ink-primary)] tracking-tight">
              2. Understanding the Age Calculator Formula (Excel & Programmatic Math)
            </h3>
            <p>
              In software engineering and spreadsheet software like Microsoft Excel, the standard <strong>age calculator in excel</strong> formula uses the hidden <code>DATEDIF</code> function:
            </p>
            <div class="p-4 bg-[var(--canvas-inset)] border-l-4 border-[#0070f3] rounded-r-lg font-mono text-xs text-[var(--ink-primary)] overflow-x-auto break-all sm:break-normal">
              =DATEDIF(start_date, end_date, "Y") &amp; " Years, " &amp; DATEDIF(start_date, end_date, "YM") &amp; " Months, " &amp; DATEDIF(start_date, end_date, "MD") &amp; " Days"
            </div>
            <p>
              Our web application executes this precise mathematical algorithm directly inside your browser without sending sensitive personal data to remote servers.
            </p>
          </section>
        </>
      )}

      {page === 'upsc' && (
        <>
          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--ink-primary)] tracking-tight">
              1. Rule 6 & The Official 1st August Cutoff Date
            </h3>
            <p>
              In India, millions of Civil Services aspirants rely on an official <strong>age calculator of upsc</strong> to verify compliance with Rule 6 of the Civil Services Examination (CSE) notification. The Union Public Service Commission specifies a fixed crucial cutoff date: <strong>1st August of the examination year</strong>.
            </p>
            <p>
              If your date of birth falls between 2nd August 1994 and 1st August 2005 (for General category in UPSC CSE 2026), you are eligible. If you turn 32 after 1st August 2026, you remain fully eligible because your age on the cutoff date was 31.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--ink-primary)] tracking-tight">
              2. Category-Wise Attempt Limits & Age Relaxations
            </h3>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-xs font-mono-num text-[var(--ink-primary)] pl-2">
              <li><strong>General / EWS:</strong> Upper age cap 32 Years (6 Attempts)</li>
              <li><strong>OBC (Non-Creamy Layer):</strong> Upper age cap 35 Years (+3 Yrs relaxation, 9 Attempts)</li>
              <li><strong>SC / ST:</strong> Upper age cap 37 Years (+5 Yrs relaxation, Unlimited Attempts)</li>
              <li><strong>PwBD Candidates:</strong> +10 Years cumulative relaxation across all categories</li>
              <li><strong>Ex-Servicemen:</strong> Up to 5 years relaxation for ECOs/SSCOs with 5+ years service</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </>
